# See https://docs.github.com/articles/about-codeowners for syntax.
# Order matters — later matches take precedence, so the generated-contract
# rules (most specific) are listed after the package-wide rules.
#
# NOTE: the thyn-ai org has exactly one member today (@0xamlab, verified
# via `gh api orgs/thyn-ai/members`) and no teams. Every entry below is that
# one real account, not a placeholder — replace with real teams
# (@thyn-ai/python-sdk-maintainers, @thyn-ai/ts-sdk-maintainers,
# @thyn-ai/platform-contract-owners) as soon as a second maintainer joins.
# Until then, do NOT turn on branch protection's "Require review from Code
# Owners" — GitHub blocks a PR author from approving their own PR, so a
# solo-owner CODEOWNERS with that setting on would make every PR unmergeable
# by the only person who can open one.

/packages/python-sdk/ @0xamlab
/packages/ts-sdk/     @0xamlab

# Generated contract snapshots — regenerated internally, never hand-edited.
# Routing these to a distinct owner means any PR touching them (accidentally
# or otherwise) gets flagged for deliberate review rather than being
# mergeable as an incidental part of a routine SDK PR.
/packages/python-sdk/decision_engine/_contract.py @0xamlab
/packages/ts-sdk/src/contract.ts                  @0xamlab

# Workflow files are as security-sensitive as the code they run.
/.github/ @0xamlab
